      <h2 id="step-3-check-your-work" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: Check your work<a href="#step-3-check-your-work" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check your work</strong>
      <p>Format each file that you changed: in the editor, choose <strong>XML</strong> &gt; <strong>Format</strong> and save the file. From the command line, format them all:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita *.ditamap"} lang="bash" />
      <p>Then check the project. In the editor, choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Check Project</strong> and read the result in the <strong>Project Validation</strong> panel. From the command line, run:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml check ."} lang="bash" />
      <p>Example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   clean\nbuild    full                 ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/full\n  5 note(s) — run with --verbose to see them\nbuild    beginner-mac         ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/beginner-mac\nbuild    beginner-windows     ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/beginner-windows\nbuild    podcaster-linux      ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/podcaster-linux\n  1 note(s) — run with --verbose to see them\nbuild    review               ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/review\n  4 note(s) — run with --verbose to see them\nbuild    install-variants     ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/install-variants\n  7 note(s) — run with --verbose to see them\nbuild    collection           ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/collection\n  18 note(s) — run with --verbose to see them\nbuild    book-pdf             ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/book-pdf\n  WARN  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-book.ditamap  PDF rendering reported 19 warnings (12 The following feature isn't implemented by Apache FOP, yet: table-layout=… (on fo:table) (…, 2 The contents of fo:inline line n exceed the available area in the inline-progression direc…, 2 The contents of fo:block line n exceed the available area in the inline-progression direct…, and 3 other kinds)\n  6 note(s) — run with --verbose to see them\noutput   wrote a file, no pages to check links in book-pdf\noutput   clean (full, beginner-mac, beginner-windows, podcaster-linux, review, install-variants, collection)\nReady: the project is healthy, every deliverable built, and the output of full, beginner-mac, beginner-windows, podcaster-linux, review, install-variants, collection holds together."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The note lines count DITA-OT notes from each build. To print them, run <code>dogsbay-xml check -v .</code>, or read them in the <strong>Project Validation</strong> panel.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>Test the position of the repetition separator. Move the <code>&lt;repsep&gt;</code> line out of the inner <code>&lt;groupseq&gt;</code> to directly after <code>&lt;delim&gt;:&lt;/delim&gt;</code> in the outer one, and check your work. The check stops at health. Example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   NOT CLEAN\n  invalid: /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/scripting-reference.dita\n    39:20  The content of element type \"groupseq\" does not match its content model.\n  (run project-health for the full report)\nNot ready: the project itself has faults. The build and the built output were not checked."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>A <code>&lt;repsep&gt;</code> follows the optional title and precedes the items in its group. The message names the element it found instead of what the model allows.</p>
      <p>Undo the change and check again. Confirm that the check reports <code>Ready</code> before you continue.</p>
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li>The programming domain: <code>&lt;syntaxdiagram&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;groupseq&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;kwd&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;delim&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;var&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;repsep&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;synph&gt;</code>; <code>&lt;parml&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;plentry&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;pt&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;pd&gt;</code>; <code>&lt;parmname&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;option&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;apiname&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;codeph&gt;</code>; <code>&lt;codeblock outputclass="language-…"&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;coderef&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>The software domain: <code>&lt;cmdname&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;varname&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;msgph&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;msgblock&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;msgnum&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;userinput&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;systemoutput&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>The user interface domain: <code>&lt;screen&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;refsyn&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;properties&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;prophead&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;property&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;proptype&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;propvalue&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;propdesc&gt;</code>, and a profiling attribute on a row.</li>
      <li>A <code>&lt;repsep&gt;</code> precedes the items in its group, after any title.</li>
      <li>Code lives in a file and the topic references it.</li>
      </ul>
